    "evidence_text": "Ron Dermer\n\n He began serving as Israel's Ambassador to the United States in October 2013.\n\nMaya Harris\n\n She was formerly a senior fellow at the Center for American Progress.\n\n From 2008 until she took her current position, she was Vice President for Democracy, Rights and Justice at the Ford Foundation.\n\nAllison Garrett\n\n Before her current position, Garrett held several vice president positions in both education and corporate jobs.\n\nTodd Philip Haskell\n\n When Trump took office, he withdrew Haskell's nomination before reinstating his nomination.\n\nThe Case for Democracy\nThe Case for Democracy is a foreign policy manifesto written by one-time Soviet political prisoner and former Israeli Member of the Knesset, Natan Sharansky.\n Sharansky's friend Ron Dermer is the book's co-author.\n The book achieved the bestsellers list of the \"New York Times\", \"Washington Post\" and \"Foreign Affairs\".\n\nTsewang Rigzin\n\n Prior to attaining his current position he served as the president of the Portland/Vancouver regional chapter of the Tibetan Youth Congress.\n\nAvital Sharansky\n\nMoving map display\n\nDefending Identity\n\nHamadou Moustapha",
